  "definition": "Meta-learning for AutoML transfers experience across datasets or tasks. Dataset meta-features and prior trials can warm-start algorithm selection, hyperparameter search, or surrogate models on a new task.",
  "intuition": "A new dataset should not start from zero when similar datasets have already been solved; reuse their metadata and trial history to get a better starting point.",
  "mathematical_foundation": "",
  "advantages": [
    "Can warm-start search with useful configurations, priors, or algorithm choices.",
    "Reduces cold-start cost by reusing experience across datasets."
  ],
